The drill is done: 14 of 15 blocks pass after 2 iterations. I could only estimate the sheet length by hand, because I had no way to count characters. My estimate is about 3.2k characters against the 3368 hard cap. Please check `agent-work/rewrite/3.2.md` with `wc -m` before splicing it in.

- **Iteration 1:** 10 of 15 pass. The 5 fails were:
  - **apr24-3d and nov19-2:** the sheet had no identity for rewriting cos3θ in terms of cosθ.
  - **pe21-3b:** the sheet never said to stop an MA(q) correlogram at lag q.
  - **pe21-3a:** the ARMA recipe covered the difference equation but not the H(z) filter form.
  - **jan19-4:** this is a Wiener-filter question, which the sheet doesn't cover.
- **Rewrite:** I added the cos3θ identity, a "stop at lag q" trigger for MA(q) correlograms, and "ρ[τ] = r[τ]". I also added a "Find a,b" trigger on the MA(2) recipe, the H(z) form mapped to β and α, and a second worked ARMA example.
- **Iteration 2:** all four fixable fails now pass. Only jan19-4 still fails, and I marked it out of scope for 3.2 (a 2019 outlier).
- **Plot-pick parts:** I couldn't test the plot-letter parts of apr25-3g and apr24-3f because I had no access to the figures. Those two blocks pass on their text parts only.

**Progress log:** `agent-work/progress/3.2.md` already held lines from an earlier run when I started. I appended my run after them rather than rewriting the file, so it has two sets of results.

